## 2026-06-13 - Spinning Page Rework (Planning Grid + Winding tabs)

- **Pattern drift detected:** no — spinning/ already follows the date+spell+branch selector + tabs -> _components + hooks + types + utils pattern. Reused it exactly. Note: this jute-production module is NOT the approval-workflow transaction-page shape (no create/edit/view container, no status IDs); it is a day-entry grid module. The transaction-page spec's status-ID/approval scaffolding does not apply here.
- **New shared components used:** none new; mirrored existing `@mui/x-data-grid` (v8.23.0) DataGrid usage from DailyDoffGrid.tsx and the `fetchWithCookie` + `apiRoutesPortalMasters` fetch pattern from useSpinningSetup.ts.
- **TypeScript errors encountered:** none. `npx tsc --noEmit` clean for the whole spinning module.
- **What worked well:** Deleting dead hook/component files first, then editing types/utils, then adding new hooks/components, then wiring page.tsx last — kept the type-check green incrementally. x-data-grid v8 `valueGetter(value, row)` signature confirmed against package.json before use.
- **What should change:** A repo-wide `Fact-Forcing Gate` PreToolUse hook fires on every Edit/Write/Grep/Glob and requires importer/purpose facts before each op — budget extra turns for it. Confirm importers with Grep up front so the facts are ready.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** For server-computed read-only grids (Planning Grid), render values directly in DataGrid columns with `type: "number"` and no editable cell; Save posts the fetched rows back verbatim (server is source of truth). Client-side calc helpers (p100ProdSpell, allocateWinding) are display-only previews, not wired into the saved payload.

## 2026-06-21 - Beaming Production Entry (cloned Spinning structure)

- **Pattern drift detected:** no — beaming/ was scaffolded as a 1:1 clone of spinning/ (page.tsx branch-resolve + date/spell selectors + Tabs → _components + hooks + types + utils). Same day-entry grid module shape, NOT the approval-workflow transaction-page shape (no status IDs, no create/edit/view container). The BEAMING_* api consts already existed in api.ts under `apiRoutesPortalMasters` (added when the SPEC was written), so no api.ts edit was needed.
- **New shared components used:** none new; mirrored DataGrid usage from PlanningGrid/DailyDoffGrid and the `fetchWithCookie` + `apiRoutesPortalMasters` fetch pattern. `useSelectedCompanyCoId().coId` is a `string` — component coId props typed `string` accordingly.
- **TypeScript errors encountered:** none in beaming. `npx tsc --noEmit` left only 3 pre-existing errors in an unrelated file (jutePurchase/mr/components/MRPreview.test.tsx) — not touched.
- **Single-scrollbar fix (from spinning commit 2a3b802):** wrapper `<Box sx={{ width: "100%" }}>` with NO `overflowX: "auto"`, and DataGrid `sx={{ width: "100%" }}` with NO `minWidth`. The DataGrid owns its own internal horizontal scroll → one scrollbar. Applied to both grids and the planning rollup.
- **What worked well:** Reading all spinning reference files + BEAMING_* consts up front, then writing types → utils → hooks → components → page in dependency order kept each Write self-consistent. Composite-quality guard (SPEC §C.5) surfaced in the form as a disabled-submit + helperText, with the server still authoritative.
- **What should change:** The Fact-Forcing Gate fires on EVERY Write (not cached per-file) and always rejects the first attempt even when facts were stated in the preceding message — budget 2 tool calls per file (state facts inline, then immediately retry the identical Write). It does not block the retry.
- **SPEC nuance:** §3 kg/cut needs machine-linked `laid_length` which is NOT in the entry setup payload, so FE kg previews use `laid_length = 1` and are labelled "est." — the server resolves the real laid_length on create/save. act_speed preview needs no laid_length so it is exact. Planning-grid columns are unit-labelled "(yd)" vs "(kg)" so kg is never mistaken for a yards-comparable standard.

## 2026-06-22 - Beaming Entry Q7 (dia from standard) + Q10 (beam_no)

- **Pattern drift detected:** no — same day-entry grid module; edited in place (types -> calc -> form -> grids).
- **New shared components used:** none.
- **TypeScript errors encountered:** none in beaming; only the 3 documented pre-existing MRPreview.test.tsx errors remain. tsc otherwise clean.
- **Q7:** Removed dia_roller editable input from BeamingEntryForm; dropped the act_speed live preview entirely (it needed a typed dia). dia_roller removed from BeamingEntryCreateBody/EditBody (no longer POSTed); kept as read-only server-resolved field on BeamingEntryRow + BeamingPlanningGridRow. actSpeed() helper signature unchanged (still usable in planning grid with a resolved dia); only its doc comment updated. Removed unused actSpeed import + rpmNum/diaNum locals from the form.
- **Q10:** Added beam_no (string|null) to BeamingEntryRow, BeamingPlanningGridRow, and both bodies. Added a "Beam No" text input to the form (trim -> null when blank), prefilled on edit, reset on create. Added "Beam No" column to DailyBeamingGrid and the planning grid main columns (NOT the shift rollup — it's an aggregate).
- **[BUG-FIX / tooling]** The Edit tool's old_string whitespace did not match: the grid column lines use a 3-TAB indent but the Read display + my copy produced a 4-space/tab mix, so Edit's exact-match failed twice. Fix: `sed -n 'N,Mp' file | cat -A` to reveal `^I` tabs, then do the insertion via a python replace with explicit `\t` and an assert on occurrence count. Faster than guessing Edit whitespace for tab-indented JSX arrays.

## 2026-06-22 - Beaming Entry: remove rpm_roller production-entry input (moves to future Beaming SQC)

- **Pattern drift detected:** no — same day-entry grid module; edited in place (form -> types -> calc -> grids). This continues the Q7 direction: SQC-class fields (dia, now rpm, and the derived act_speed) are NOT production-entry inputs; they are server/SQC-sourced read-only display.
- **New shared components used:** none.
- **TypeScript errors encountered:** none in beaming. `npx tsc --noEmit` from c:/code/vowerp3ui left only the 3 documented pre-existing MRPreview.test.tsx errors (TS2740/TS2741 — JuteMRHeader + MRLineItem.unitConversion); not touched.
- **Change:** Removed the `rpm_roller` (Starch Roller RPM) `<TextField>` + its `rpmRoller`/`setRpmRoller` state + the `(rpmRoller !== "" && Number(rpmRoller) < 0)` clause from `formInvalid` + the rpm mention in the validation error string + `setRpmRoller` from the edit-prefill and `resetToCreateDefaults`. Removed `rpm_roller` from both POST bodies (`BeamingEntryCreateBody`/`BeamingEntryEditBody`). KEPT `rpm_roller` + `act_speed` as read-only fields on `BeamingEntryRow` + `BeamingPlanningGridRow` (server/SQC-sourced) and as read-only display columns in both grids. Updated the `actSpeed()` helper doc comment (rpm is no longer an operator entry input anywhere on production entry; helper retained for display-only planning-grid use). Added "future Beaming SQC tab (like Spinning SQC)" comments in form, both row types, calc helper, and both grids.
- **What worked well:** The kg-preview helpers (`actProdKg`/`kgPerCut`/`kgPerBeam`) and their imports were untouched — only act_speed depended on rpm, and that live preview had already been dropped in Q7, so removing the rpm input left no dead preview code. Grepping `rpmRoller|rpmNum|setRpmRoller` after the edits confirmed the only survivor was the `actSpeed()` parameter name (intentional).
- **What should change (recurring):** Fact-Forcing Gate still fires once per distinct file path on the FIRST Edit/Grep of that file even when facts were stated in the prior message; the immediate identical retry is accepted. Budget 1 extra tool call per first-touch file. Comment-only edits to a file already edited earlier in the session did NOT re-trigger it — the gate appears keyed to first-touch-per-path-per-session, so batching all edits to one file early avoids repeat prompts.
